                <pb facs="0362" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.5151/419: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Buenos Aires</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-15T17:00:00-04:00">April 15, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 15—4:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to my telegram of April 14, noon. The increase in cost to importers
                    without advance exchange permits according to the terms of the decree is
                    computed as follows: the percent difference between the Banco Nación average
                    rate for accepted bids for official exchange and its closing free selling rate
                    on the previous day will be deducted from 20 percent. The percent difference
                    will be applied as a surcharge on the c. i. f. value of imports.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
